.TH "sudoconsole" "1" "Aug 2026" "sudoconsole " "sudoconsole Manual"

.SH NAME
sudoconsole-detect - Detect installed CLI agents on the host


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsudoconsole detect [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
detect scans the host for supported CLI agents (Kilo, Claude Code,
Gemini, Aider, Codex, Copilot). Each probe runs in parallel with a
2-second budget so a slow PATH lookup never blocks the call. Use
--json to feed the result into scripts.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for detect


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--cache-timeout\fP=0
	sudo cache timeout in seconds (60-3600); overrides config file

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the TOML config file (default: platform XDG/Application Support location)

.PP
\fB--format\fP=""
	output format: human or json (overrides config file)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP=""
	log level: silent, error, warn, info, debug (overrides config file)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sudoconsole detect
  sudoconsole --format json detect
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsudoconsole(1)\fP


